### Movement states

The player controller should support:

| Category    | Movement states                              |
| ----------- | -------------------------------------------- |
| Ground      | Idle, walk, jog, sprint                      |
| Directional | Forward, backward, strafe, diagonal          |
| Terrain     | Uphill, downhill, slopes, uneven ground      |
| Traversal   | Jump, fall, land, climb, vault               |
| Water       | Enter, swim, dive, surface, exit             |
| Combat      | Combat idle, combat walk, dodge, roll, block |
| Interaction | Open, pull, push, carry, gather              |
| Conditions  | Injured, exhausted, frozen, poisoned         |

Movement transitions should blend smoothly without making the player feel sluggish.

### Movement mathematics

Define movement speed:

V = V_b \\times M_{\\text{state}} \\times M_{\\text{terrain}}
\\times M_{\\text{condition}}

Where:

* : base movement speed.

* : walking, sprinting, swimming, and other state multipliers.

* : terrain influence.

* : effects of stamina, injuries, and status conditions.

Acceleration:

a = \\frac{V_{\\text{target}}-V_{\\text{current}}}{t}

Slope influence:

M_{\\text{slope}} =
\\operatorname{Clamp}(1-k\\sin(\\theta),M_{\\min},M_{\\max})

These are starting mathematical models. Final coefficients must be tuned through gameplay testing.

### 3\. Advanced animation architecture

Build one unified animation framework rather than independent animation controllers for every character.

### Aetheria Animation Architecture

Character or Creature Controller

Input, AI commands, gameplay state

Animation State Manager

Movement, combat, interactions, reactions

Animator State Machines

Blend Trees

Animation Layers

Procedural Animation

IK & Rigging

Root Motion

Unity Character Presentation

Animation, movement, physics, audio, VFX and camera feedback

### Animation layers

Create independent layers for:

* Full-body locomotion.

* Upper-body weapon handling.

* Facial expression.

* Head and eye tracking.

* Equipment and weapon handling.

* Hit reactions.

* Environmental interactions.

* Special abilities.

Layer blending must avoid conflicting animations and unintended skeletal deformation.

### 4\. Advanced combat animation

Combat animation must connect directly to the combat formulas and hit detection systems developed in the previous formula specification.

