### Animation-driven combat timing

Every attack should have defined timing windows:

T_{\\text{attack}} =
T_{\\text{startup}}+T_{\\text{active}}+T_{\\text{recovery}}

During the active window, the combat system enables the relevant hit detection.

Important requirements:

* No damage during invalid attack windows.

* No duplicate damage from one attack unless intentionally designed.

* Animation cancellation follows gameplay rules.

* Weapon trails synchronize with attack motion.

* Hit reactions depend on impact direction and strength.

* Boss attacks have clear visual warning animations.

