12. Regression testing and documentation.

Do not implement everything as one enormous script.

Do not create duplicate systems when suitable implementations already exist.

## 13. ACCEPTANCE CRITERIA

V11 is complete only when:

- The player has functional movement animation.
- Movement transitions are responsive.
- Combat animations synchronize with validated gameplay windows.
- Enemy and boss reactions work.
- Existing companions, creatures, and mounts remain compatible.
- IK works on appropriate supported rigs.
- Facial animation works on supported characters.
- Blender exports pass validation.
- The Animation Studio functions.
- Animation performance has been profiled.
- World streaming does not break animation state.
- Existing gameplay systems continue to work.
- Documentation and automated tests are included.

## FINAL RULE

Preserve Aetheria's established world, characters, mechanics, assets, progression, and single-player identity.

Inspect first. Plan second. Implement third. Test continuously. Do not fabricate completed work or replace established game design with invented content.

V11's central goal: make Aetheria's characters feel physically believable and responsive, while keeping animation tightly connected to movement, combat, creature behavior, and the world itself.
